From 98206e643551bd5881aebe5da68023e3e61dc671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:31:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Chain authority: estimateGas answers a gas limit a verified
 execution succeeded with

The pinned Helios answers eth_estimateGas with the gas USED after refunds,
and answers even for a failing call. A release frees storage, so sent with
that limit it ran out of gas on chain (every release in the consumer E2E
reverted). Search the limit with verified eth_call executions at one numbered
block instead: the call must succeed at the cap (else its revert is the
answer), the verifier's used gas is the lower bound, and the answer is
always a limit at which a verified execution succeeded (within 1.5%).
The release resolver's note now carries the RPC details.
---
